.TH MU2EDAQ_CLI_CORE 3 "2026-07-27" "mu2edaq-commandline-tools 0.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ C++ API"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq_cli_core \- C++ configuration helpers for the Mu2e DAQ command line tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <mu2edaq_cli_core.hpp>
.PP
.B namespace mu2edaq { namespace cli {
.PP
.BI "const char* version();"
.BI "const char* env_prefix();"
.BI "std::vector<std::string> config_search_paths(const std::string& " explicit_path " = \"\");"
.BI "std::string find_config(const std::string& " explicit_path " = \"\");"
.BI "std::string env_override(const std::string& " key ", const std::string& " fallback " = \"\");"
.PP
.B }}
.fi
.PP
Link with
.BR -lmu2edaq_cli_core ,
or, with this checkout added to your build:
.PP
.RS
.nf
add_subdirectory(mu2edaq-commandline-tools)
target_link_libraries(mytool PRIVATE mu2edaq::cli_core)
.fi
.RE
.SH DESCRIPTION
This library gives C++ tools the same configuration lookup the Python package
uses, so a C++ tool and a Python tool started from the same directory read the
same YAML file. It does not parse YAML; it locates the file and reads the
environment. Pick your own parser for the contents.
.TP
.B version()
Package version string, e.g.
.BR 0.1.0 .
Compiled in from the Python package's
.I __version__
at configure time, so the two cannot drift.
.TP
.B env_prefix()
The environment variable prefix,
.BR MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_ .
.TP
.B config_search_paths()
Candidate config file locations, most specific first. When
.I explicit_path
is non-empty it is the only candidate returned. Otherwise the order is
.BR $MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_CONFIG ", "
.IR ./mu2edaq-commandline-tools.yaml ", "
.IR ./config/mu2edaq-commandline-tools.yaml ", "
.IR ~/.config/mu2edaq/commandline-tools.yaml ", "
.IR /etc/mu2edaq/commandline-tools.yaml .
Paths are returned whether or not they exist.
.TP
.B find_config()
The first candidate that is an existing regular file, or an empty string if
none is. An empty return is not an error: the defaults are usable on their own.
.TP
.B env_override()
The value of
.BI MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_ KEY
with
.I key
upper-cased and dashes turned into underscores, or
.I fallback
when the variable is unset or empty.
.SH RETURN VALUE
No function throws or returns an error code. Filesystem errors during the
search are treated as "not found".
.SH THREAD SAFETY
All functions are reentrant but read the process environment and current
working directory, so results change if another thread calls
.BR setenv (3)
or
.BR chdir (2)
concurrently.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
#include <mu2edaq_cli_core.hpp>
#include <iostream>

int main() {
  const std::string cfg = mu2edaq::cli::find_config();
  if (cfg.empty()) std::cout << "using built-in defaults\\n";
  else             std::cout << "config: " << cfg << "\\n";
  const std::string cluster = mu2edaq::cli::env_override("cluster", "mu2edaq");
  std::cout << "cluster: " << cluster << "\\n";
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq-tools-info (1),
.BR mu2edaq-tools (1),
.BR mu2edaq_commandline_tools (3)
